# Tape-head saturation validation circuit (engine side).
#
# Minimal standalone circuit that drives a single voltage-driven Jiles-Atherton
# tape head from a line-level source through a build-out resistor into a load.
# The head colours on its GAP VOLTAGE (H = kv*V), so it reaches its J-A knee at
# ~1 V line level and THD climbs with drive — the property this test validates
# against an ngspice behavioural J-A reference (see
# spice-circuits/tape/tape_head_saturation.spice).
#
# TOPOLOGY — the head is a nonlinear SHUNT load on the output node, exactly as
# the ngspice golden deck models it ("head sinks i(V) at v_out"):
#
#   in --[R_pri 470Ω]--> out ;  R_load(2.2k): out --> gnd ;  TH: out --> gnd
#
# The head's WDF port voltage V is therefore V(out) (port across out->gnd), so
# H = kv*V(out) drives saturation off the actual output level — matching the
# deck's `Bhead v_out 0 I = Gp*V(v_out) + Isat*M/Ms` shunt and `R_load v_out 0`.
#
# NOTE (bead pedalkernel-x0mv, Phase 0): this circuit previously wired TH in
# SERIES between R_pri.b and out, which made the head port voltage the series
# drop V(R_pri.b)-V(out) rather than V(out). That series topology does NOT match
# the shunt golden deck and produced a ~4 dB clean-regime level error — a netlist
# mismatch, NOT an element-model defect. Instrumenting the compiled circuit vs
# the ngspice golden sample-by-sample confirmed the shunt netlist matches the
# golden to ~70 dB (clean AND saturated); the J-A element is unchanged. With this
# stiff 470/2.2k divider the head is a light shunt load, so output THD is modest
# (≤~1.2%, matching ngspice ground truth) — a faithful, mild-saturation reference.
#
# The head is the only nonlinear element; everything else is a plain resistor,
# so an ngspice B-source J-A head produces a directly comparable V(out).
#
# Head model = the shipped STUDIO-HEAD defaults (compiler/components/tape_head.rs
# ::studio_head, mirrored explicitly in the .spice .param block):
#   Ms=3.5e5 A/m, a=1500, alpha=1.6e-3, k=30, c=0.65,
#   kv=8000 A/m/V, Isat=200 uA, Gp=80 uS, h_bias=400 A/m, Rp=1 kΩ.

pedal "Tape Head Saturation" {
  components {
    R_pri:  resistor(470)        # head build-out / source impedance
    TH:     tape_head()          # voltage-driven Jiles-Atherton tape head
    R_load: resistor(2.2k)       # head load
  }
  nets {
    in -> R_pri.a
    R_pri.b -> out, TH.a, R_load.a
    TH.b -> gnd
    R_load.b -> gnd
  }
}
